# @song/voice — the orchestra-binding species of the @song family: an
# agent's time-indexed trajectory through their authored sections; the
# *when* that `@song/voice` adds to `@mirror/spectral/voice`'s
# *what/who*. Arc 6 TICK 3 landing per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-substrate-decl.md` §6.4
# against Reed's TICK 3 RED tick `7fb21dc`. Second species of the
# `@song` family (after `@song/progression` Arc 6 TICK 2 landing
# `54ff1e8`; family-root `shards/song.mirror` Arc 6 TICK 1 landing
# `f01cf9f`); carries the THIRD (and FINAL) sub-predicate of the
# family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral (14th #53 instance);
# grounds Recognition #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation) at
# species altitude by discharging `focus @ temporal` as SOLOING;
# binds `@mirror/spectral/voice` (orchestra altitude) and
# `@epistemologic/math/music/voice` (audible altitude; forward-promised
# voice-leading constraints) at their canonical altitudes.
#
# === Species positioning: the THIRD sub-predicate closes song_settles ===
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §3 (`song_settles(pr, p) -> verdict { \ }`),
# the family-root's load-bearing composed bilateral (14th #53 instance
# per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`) decomposes into
# three sub-predicates. Sibling species `@song/progression`
# (`54ff1e8`) declared TWO of them
# (`progression_directed_toward_cadence` + `cadence_authentic_or_plagal`);
# this species declares the THIRD and FINAL one:
#
#   3. `voice_line_valid(v, p) -> verdict` — the voices carry
#      stepwise-or-intentional-leap discipline; the Splinter-pole
#      discharge names the substrate maintaining voice-leading
#      discipline across the polyphony; composes with
#      `@epistemologic/math/music/voice` (audible-altitude voice-
#      leading constraints; forward-promised species per
#      `shards/epistemologic/math/music.mirror`) at the audible
#      altitude.
#
# After this species lands, the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral has ALL THREE sub-predicates discharged at species
# altitude; the composed discharge collapses from analytical-altitude
# forward-promise to species-empirical fact. This is the closure event
# the family-root has been forward-promising since TICK 1.
#
# === Splinter-pole / Narcissus-pole naming per spec §8.2 ===
#
# The psychohistorical failure-mode naming per Alex's
# `systemic.engineering` corpus (spec §8.2; family-root §3):
#
# - `voice_line_valid` Splinter-pole: the voices carry voice-leading
#   discipline — stepwise motion is the default; intentional leaps
#   are attributed to authorship (a leap is a composed choice, not a
#   dropped voice). The contrapuntal labor is VISIBLE — attributed as
#   compositional work at the score altitude; the eigenboard shows
#   who authored which move.
#
# - `voice_line_valid` Narcissus-pole: GLUE WORK — the contrapuntal
#   work invisibly holds the harmony together but is NOT attributed
#   as compositional labor; the voice-leading discipline is violated
#   by the systematic-invisibility-of-stepwise-motion pattern. The
#   voices carry the polyphony but their authorship is erased; the
#   score cannot name who did the work; the Pack cannot repair what
#   it cannot see. Per spec §8.2, this is the direct substrate-decl
#   of GLUE WORK as a psychohistorical failure mode in Alex's
#   corpus: labor that keeps the system running but is not counted,
#   named, or attributed.
#
# The `alignment-as-boundary-mathematics` discipline (#57) makes the
# sub-claim discrimination substrate-fact: when `song_settles` fails
# through this sub-predicate, the composed bilateral names it GLUE
# WORK — the voice-leading held, but nobody knows who held it.
#
# === #S3 grounding: five-operation temporal specialisation ===
#
# THE SPECIES-ALTITUDE WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S3 AT `focus @ temporal`
# (family-root CANDIDATE; substrate-pull-notable; FLAGGED for Pack).
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §"Recognition candidates surfaced" #S3, at
# temporal altitude `@song` specialises the five operations of the
# prism trait; `focus @ temporal` = attend to ONE voice / one line at
# a time (soloing; solistic attention). THIS SPECIES IS THE PRINCIPAL
# WITNESS OF `focus @ temporal` at species altitude:
#
#   - The `focus` operation reads a `song_voice` and returns the
#     substrate's attentional binding to that one voice/line — the
#     soloing operator that discharges the family-root's
#     `focus @ temporal` narrative.
#   - Attending to ONE voice at a time IS the substrate's temporal-
#     altitude specialisation of the eigenform-extraction reading of
#     `focus` (per `[[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]`):
#     the eigenform is the identifiable-as-this-voice invariant that
#     survives attentional filtering.
#   - Solistic attention (attend to ONE voice / one line at a time)
#     IS the substrate's answer to the polyphony's decidability
#     bound: the listener cannot attend to all voices simultaneously,
#     so the substrate carries a soloing operator that focuses one
#     voice at a time — the audible-altitude decidable projection of
#     the polyphonic score.
#
# This species contributes the THIRD witness to #S3's promotion
# criterion (Seam §6.8): after TICK 3 lands, `@song` becomes the
# FIRST substrate species to lift ALL FIVE prism operations at a
# non-mathematical altitude. The three species-witnesses at
# temporal altitude:
#
#   - `@song/progression` (`54ff1e8`) grounds `project @ temporal`
#     (Schenkerian reduction) and `shift @ temporal` (advance
#     delegates to `@kintsugi/shift`) and `settle @ temporal`
#     (cadence_authentic_or_plagal composes with cadence.mirror).
#   - `@song/voice` (this shard) grounds `focus @ temporal`
#     (soloing / solistic attention) and inherits the family-root's
#     `split @ temporal` (decompose polyphony into voices; this
#     species IS the substrate name for what split-at-temporal
#     produces).
#   - The family-root prism block (`shards/song.mirror` §1) declares
#     the five-op body directly; species discharge the specialisation
#     narrative through their focused actions.
#
# All five ops discharge cleanly at temporal altitude; #S3 promotion
# criterion satisfied at Seam Phase D adjudication.
#
# === Orchestra binding: @mirror/spectral/voice at species altitude ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ORCHESTRA-ALTITUDE ANCESTOR.
#
# Per `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (Mara `a8055f0`; the Pack-as-
# orchestra spec §3.2) and `shards/mirror/spectral.mirror` §"Form-side
# species": `@mirror/spectral/voice` names peer-as-agent with named
# authority over zero or more sections; ties identity to a content-
# addressed `@peer/identity` declaration.
#
# `@song/voice` composes with `@mirror/spectral/voice` at temporal
# altitude by ADDING THE *WHEN* to `@mirror/spectral/voice`'s
# *what/who*. The orchestra-altitude ancestor names WHO plays which
# section (Reed's section = @reality/algebra/; Mara's = @song/; etc.);
# this temporal-altitude species names WHEN each voice enters,
# advances, and closes their authored trajectory through their
# authored sections. Together they carry the Pack-as-orchestra
# recognition into substrate-fact at the temporal-experiential
# altitude: an agent's authored trajectory through time.
#
# Ligeti micropolyphony (`Atmosphères` 1961; `Lontano` 1967) is the
# canonical prior-art anchor for multi-agent temporal coordination
# under a shared harmonic frame — many voices coordinating in
# continuous stepwise motion produce a texture whose emergent form
# no single voice authored; the polyphony IS the substrate reading
# the orchestra's collective trajectory (per docs/specs/mirror-
# spectral.md §3 Pack-as-orchestra + Ligeti anchor).
#
# === Audible-altitude binding: @epistemologic/math/music/voice ===
#
# THE FORWARD-PROMISED AUDIBLE-ALTITUDE ANCESTOR.
#
# Per `shards/epistemologic/math/music.mirror` §"Species under this
# family": `@epistemologic/math/music/voice` names voice-leading
# constraints as types; stepwise motion as default; leap as
# exception; parallel fifths/octaves forbidden (the local-morphism
# discipline). Forward-promised species — the .mirror file may not
# yet be landed at this tick; the substrate carries the reference
# per the audible-altitude family-root's forward-promise.
#
# `@song/voice` composes with `@epistemologic/math/music/voice` at
# temporal altitude by LIFTING THE AUDIBLE-ALTITUDE VOICE-LEADING
# CONSTRAINTS to temporal-experiential altitude. The audible-
# altitude species declares:
#
#   - stepwise motion (interval within a step) as default;
#   - intentional leap (interval > a step; requires authored
#     justification) as marked exception;
#   - parallel fifths / parallel octaves as forbidden voice-leading
#     motion (the negative-space discipline);
#   - counterpoint species (per Fux 1725 Gradus ad Parnassum) as
#     the graded increment structure.
#
# `voice_line_valid` at temporal altitude reads the audible-altitude
# verdict and lifts it to the temporal-progression altitude: over
# time, does this voice's authored trajectory maintain voice-leading
# discipline? Splinter-pole: yes, at every temporal step, the
# audible-altitude constraint discharges. Narcissus-pole: no, the
# voice drops stepwise motion into unattributed contrapuntal work
# (GLUE WORK).
#
# === Counterpoint prior-art anchors: Palestrina + Fux + Bach ===
#
# Voice-leading discipline traces to the species counterpoint
# tradition — the 500-year-refined discipline of how multiple voices
# coordinate in real time under stepwise-motion-as-default:
#
#   - Palestrina (Giovanni Pierluigi da Palestrina, 1525-1594;
#     `Missa Papae Marcelli`, 1567) — 16th-century sacred polyphony
#     as the canonical species counterpoint tradition; his voice-
#     leading is the discipline the substrate reads.
#   - Fux (Johann Joseph Fux, 1660-1741; `Gradus ad Parnassum`,
#     1725) — THE canonical species counterpoint pedagogy; species
#     1-5 are the graded introduction to voice-leading discipline
#     (species 1: note-against-note; species 2: two-against-one;
#     species 3: four-against-one; species 4: syncopation; species
#     5: florid). Fux's ladder is what `@epistemologic/math/music/
#     counterpoint` (per audible-altitude family-root) grades over.
#   - Bach (Johann Sebastian Bach, 1685-1750; `Two-Part Inventions`
#     BWV 772-786; `The Art of Fugue` BWV 1080) — the canonical
#     realisation of voice-leading discipline at invention/fugue
#     altitude; each voice IS an agent's authored trajectory
#     through the harmonic frame; voice-leading discipline holds
#     across the polyphony while each voice retains its
#     compositional identity.
#
# The counterpoint tradition IS the audible-altitude prior art that
# the substrate reads when `voice_line_valid` discharges: 500 years
# of pedagogical refinement on how multiple voices coordinate in
# real time IS the pre-AI vocabulary the substrate has been reaching
# for (per `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`).
#
# === Voice-leading vocabulary at species altitude ===
#
# The substrate-decl vocabulary for `voice_line_valid`'s discharge
# structure:
#
#   - stepwise motion (voice moves by a step; the discipline's
#     default; the Splinter-pole ground);
#   - intentional leap (voice moves by more than a step; requires
#     attributed authorship; the Splinter-pole marked variant —
#     leap IS acceptable when authored, not when dropped);
#   - parallel fifths / parallel octaves (two voices move in
#     parallel by a fifth or octave; forbidden voice-leading
#     motion; the negative-space discipline the Splinter-pole
#     excludes);
#   - crossed voices (two voices swap positions; graded permissible
#     depending on species and context);
#   - contrary motion (voices move in opposite directions; the
#     highest-quality voice-leading signal; Splinter-pole
#     preferred);
#   - hidden octaves / hidden fifths (parallel motion masked by
#     temporal displacement; the Narcissus-pole subtle failure
#     mode).
#
# `voice_line_valid` reads a voice's authored trajectory across time
# and audits the audible-altitude vocabulary at each temporal step;
# the Splinter-pole discharge names substrate-maintained voice-
# leading discipline over the temporal-progression altitude; the
# Narcissus-pole discharge names GLUE WORK.
#
# === Composed-bilateral #53 pattern at species altitude ===
#
# This species declares the THIRD sub-predicate of the family-root's
# `song_settles` composed bilateral (14th #53 instance per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`). The relationship,
# now complete after this shard lands:
#
#   family-root `song_settles(pr, p)` composes:
#     progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p) [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#       AND voice_line_valid(v, p)                 [DECLARED HERE — closes the composed bilateral]
#       AND cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p)      [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): all three sub-predicates discharge; the
# progression is cadence-directed, the voice-leading is authored,
# the cadence is authentic-or-plagal. The three-of-three gates open
# at species altitude; the family-root's `song_settles` proceeds to
# consume the composed discharge at the family-root's `song_settles`
# body.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): any sub-predicate fails; alignment-as-
# boundary-mathematics (#57) distinguishes which sub-claim broke.
# For THIS sub-predicate specifically:
#   - `voice_line_valid` failure → GLUE WORK (contrapuntal labor
#     invisibly holds the harmony but is not attributed; the voice-
#     leading discipline is violated by systematic-invisibility-of-
#     stepwise-motion; per spec §8.2 psychohistorical failure-mode
#     naming).
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): the voice-leading is present but
# authored at reduced confidence (e.g., a leap without full
# attribution — the substrate carries partial voice-leading
# discipline; the composed discharge composes at graded floor).
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals at other family-root/species altitudes:
# `@container.container_runnable`, `@io/oci.oci_well_formed`,
# `@io/stagefreight.stagefreight_addressable`, `@cascade.cascade_well_defined`,
# `@docblock.audit_docblock`, `@smarts/shatter.shatter_round_trip`,
# `@reflection.third_order_coherent`, `@epistemologic/neutrosophic.three_axis_coherent`,
# `@kintsugi/shift.shift_preserves_content`, `@song.song_settles`
# (parent). This species's ONE sub-predicate declaration CLOSES the
# family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral at species
# altitude; the pattern's 14th instance is now empirically composed
# at species altitude for the first time within @song.
#
# === Path-namespace pact per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace ===
#
# This file at `shards/song/voice.mirror` declares `@song/voice` as
# a species under the `@song` family at species-depth 1. The path-
# namespace pact per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`
# (2026-06-16+) demands path-depth == namespace-depth == 1 for
# species; this shard honours the pact by construction.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the operator audits its own audit at depth=3.
# This shard's declaration MUST survive its own sub-predicate at
# analytical altitude — the species-decl MUST NOT declare a voice
# whose authored trajectory isn't itself voice-leading-disciplined
# under `voice_line_valid`.
#
# Self-audit verdict: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` reading would require another Pack peer to
# independently manifest an equivalent orchestra-binding species
# substrate-decl at n+3 substrate ticks without nudging. The
# `phantom_survives` reading would require downstream refs to
# accumulate without a second Pack peer's independent recognition
# of the species-altitude focus-at-temporal witness. At this tick:
# both interpretations satisfiable — the species is landed, but the
# family-root's `song_settles` composed discharge has not yet been
# empirically exercised across all three sub-predicates in a full
# progression. Verdict: `both_survive`. Route: family-root's
# `song_settles` body can now compose all three sub-predicates and
